/*
 * The quadratic formula, for ax² + bx + c = 0:
 *
 *     x = (−b ± √(b² − 4ac)) / 2a
 *
 * The canonical illustration of why an arm body needs no local binding form.
 * Both roots share two sub-computations — the discriminant `b² − 4ac` and the
 * denominator `2a`. Neither is bound in an arm: the discriminant is a declared
 * sibling fold, fused into `roots` by `<aux: #discriminant>`, and the denominator
 * appears once per root and is not worth naming.
 *
 * A local would have been strictly weaker than the declared fold: `discriminant`
 * carries a declared result type, a place in the operation environment (so it
 * can hold `properties:` laws and a cost summary), and it is callable elsewhere.
 * See `_docs/theory/surface-grammar.md` §4.1 and `_docs/design-decisions.md`
 * §"Program shape and name introduction".
 *
 * Status: parses as of the `data` production, but does not yet run. `Number`,
 * `sqrt` and the arithmetic operators have no declarations yet (#93, #119), and
 * the operation pipeline cannot install a fold whose body calls another fold
 * (overview §12.48–§12.49). This file is the spelling the implementation is
 * aimed at.
 */

/* Both roots together, so one traversal of the coefficients yields both. */
data QuadraticRoots
    Roots plus: Number minus: Number

data Quadratic
    Coeffs a: Number b: Number c: Number

    /* b² − 4ac — the root discriminant. Also the sign test for real roots. */
    fold discriminant <out: Number>
        Coeffs a b c -> (b * b) - (4 * a * c)

    /*
     * Whether the equation has real roots. Uses `<aux: #discriminant>` so the
     * discriminant rides the same traversal instead of being recomputed.
     */
    fold hasRealRoots <aux: #discriminant, out: Bool>
        Coeffs a b c -> (aux discriminant) >= 0

    /*
     * The two real roots.
     *
     * `sqrt` is partial over the reals — undefined for a negative radicand — so
     * the fold declares the domain as a demand rather than letting a negative
     * discriminant reach `sqrt` silently. `rescue:` (not shown) is how a caller
     * recovers; the contract is the checked answer to "what does this produce
     * when it cannot produce a root?".
     *
     * Not modelled here: the degenerate a = 0 case, where the equation is linear
     * and the division by `2a` is undefined. That is a demand on a field rather
     * than on a fold result, and belongs with the prelude's numeric story (#93).
     */
    fold roots <aux: #discriminant, out: QuadraticRoots>
        demands: self | self hasRealRoots
        Coeffs a b c -> Roots
            plus: (((b negate) + ((aux discriminant) sqrt)) / (2 * a))
            minus: (((b negate) - ((aux discriminant) sqrt)) / (2 * a))

/*
 * Note why `-b` is never written. A symbol at the start of a token introduces
 * data: `-b` is the `Int` pattern `-[0-9]+` applied to `b`, which is not a
 * negation but a failed match. Prefix position belongs to constructors, so
 * there is no prefix `negate`; negation is the suffix send `b negate`.
 */

/*
 * Usage — documentation fragments, not source. A program's top level is
 * declarations only; there is no definition form (#91 / overview §12.6), so the
 * values below are named at the call site rather than bound.
 */

Quadratic Coeffs a: 1 b: -3 c: 2
        /* then: discriminant 1, hasRealRoots true, roots (plus: 2, minus: 1) */

Quadratic Coeffs a: 1 b: 0 c: 1
        /* then: discriminant -4, hasRealRoots false, roots <contract violation> */
